{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"cef65017-66a5-43fd-b15c-3a1a683b245d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The stub and cleanup script are gone (git status shows only tests/server/ untracked, which contains our test file). Good.\n\nNow a subtle issue: the autouse session fixture named `server` takes `tmp_path_factory`. If the product is delivered but server/ exists, it runs. Fine.\n\nOne more thought: `_invite_validator` inserting ROOT at sys.path every parametrized call; minor. Fine.\n\nPotential concern: `pytest.importorskip(\"yaml\")` — if PyYAML is missing, schema tests skip entirely after asserting status; 401 code assertion runs before schema? Order in test: status, schema, code. If schema skips, code assertion never runs even though it's independent. Better order: status, assert body.get(\"code\"), then schema. That way error code check still runs without jsonschema. For health/version, route length can be checked without schema. Reorder: assert code first, then schema. Small improvement. Let's do that so behavior tests are meaningful even without test deps.\n\nAlso for `test_health_with_token`: assert len routes == 1 before schema. Version: no independent assertion besides schema; fine.\n\nEdit.","signature":"cef65017-66a5-43fd-b15c-3a1a683b245d"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1397,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":38400,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8aecac3-2429-4d90-a000-406275e88d92","uuid":"8b81e12b-880a-4927-a008-bf078e78da2a","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:01:04.303Z","thinking_duration_ms":1903,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"cef65017-66a5-43fd-b15c-3a1a683b245d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-flash","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_UfmtUkCea1VXH17oxt1A7057","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/box/osaka/wt/tests/tests/server/server-core/test_server_core.py","old_string":"def test_missing_token_is_401_unauthenticated(server, path):\n    status, body = _get(path, server)\n    assert status == 401\n    _assert_schema(\"ErrorBody\", body)\n    assert body[\"code\"] == \"UNAUTHENTICATED\"\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"path\", [\"/v1/health\", \"/v1/version\"])\ndef test_wrong_token_is_403_forbidden(server, path):\n    status, body = _get(path, server, token=\"wrong-token-obviously-fake\")\n    assert status == 403\n    _assert_schema(\"ErrorBody\", body)\n    assert body[\"code\"] == \"FORBIDDEN\"\n\n\ndef test_health_with_token(server):\n    status, body = _get(\"/v1/health\", server, token=ADMIN_TOKEN)\n    assert status == 200\n    _assert_schema(\"HealthResponse\", body)\n    assert len(body[\"routes\"]) == 1","new_string":"def test_missing_token_is_401_unauthenticated(server, path):\n    status, body = _get(path, server)\n    assert status == 401\n    assert body[\"code\"] == \"UNAUTHENTICATED\"\n    _assert_schema(\"ErrorBody\", body)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"path\", [\"/v1/health\", \"/v1/version\"])\ndef test_wrong_token_is_403_forbidden(server, path):\n    status, body = _get(path, server, token=\"wrong-token-obviously-fake\")\n    assert status == 403\n    assert body[\"code\"] == \"FORBIDDEN\"\n    _assert_schema(\"ErrorBody\", body)\n\n\ndef test_health_with_token(server):\n    status, body = _get(\"/v1/health\", server, token=ADMIN_TOKEN)\n    assert status == 200\n    assert len(body[\"routes\"]) == 1\n    _assert_schema(\"HealthResponse\", body)"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1397,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens"